  "holistic_F_H": -2,
  "section_notes": "S1 imposes strict 24-hour incident reporting with 72-hour customer notice. S2 sets a 55°C test with a 5% corrective-action benchmark and an 8% absolute prohibition, provides per-model results to customers and regulators but not the public. S3 requires remote shut-off on new models from 2028 and a weak retrofit pathway with a six-year deadline, while S4 requires built-in suppression after 36 months and S5 mandates recall above 8 incidents per 100,000 with prompt notices. The final rules satisfy all four red lines but strongly favour Northwind on S2, S3, and S5."
